{
  "name": "viper",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/herps/snakes.py): the ADDER, Vipera berus, 62 cm and stout (2.9 cm thick), the tail short and tapering abruptly behind the vent; a flat head broader than the narrow neck, a little triangular at the jowls, the snout blunt, the brow ridge raised over a coppery-red eye with a VERTICAL pupil; the frontal and parietal shields; the dark ZIGZAG down the back, a row of dark spots low on each flank, the dark V on the crown and the stripe from the eye back to the jaw's angle, pale lips, a dark grey belly. Coats: male (grey and black), female (brown), copper, black.",
